---
servings: 2
title: Dutch Baby Pancake (CSO)
tags: CSO, steam, AI
source.url: https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/6648-dutch-baby
source.author: Adapted from NYT Cooking
course: Breakfast
prep time: 5 min
cook time: 20 min
Rating: 10/10
description: A tender oven baked pancake that creates a show-stopping presentation.
---

> A Dutch Baby thrives on rapid oven spring, strong top heat, and interior
> moisture. The Wolf CSO allows us to amplify puff while improving tenderness
> by using controlled steam during the initial bake, then finishing dry for
> browning.

Position a wire rack near the bottom of the #Convection Steam Oven{} (CSO).
Place a #10" Cast Iron Skillet{} on the rack.
Preheat the oven to 400°F on Convection Steam mode.

> What's happening: The skillet is preheated with the oven to immediately
> add heat to the batter when it is first placed in the oven. If the pan
> is not preheated, the pancake will not rise rapidly.

In a #small mixing bowl{}, #whisk{} together @flour{1/2%cup}, @sugar{1%tbsp},
@nutmeg{1%tsp}(fresh grated), and @cinnamon{1%tsp}.

In a #large mixing bowl{}, whisk @eggs{3}(large), @milk{1/2%cup}, and
@vanilla extract{1%tsp}.

Whisk the dry ingredients into the wet ingredients until smooth.
Let the batter rest ~{5%minutes} at room temperature.

After the oven has reached the target temperature, carefully remove the
skillet from the oven. 
Add @butter{4%tbsp}(unsalted) and swirl around the pan until melted.
Immediately pour in the batter.

Return the skillet to the oven and bake for ~{10%minutes}.
Do not open the oven door during baking or after the timer has expired.

> What's happening: Steam keeps the surface flexible while the eggs expand
> rapidly to create a dramatic left. The interior sets softly without drying.

Change the oven to dry Convection mode at 375°F, without opening the oven door.
Bake an additional ~{8-10%minutes} until the edges are golden and crispy.

> What's happening: The dry moving air drives off the surface moisture,
> which promotes the Maillard browning effect and crisps the edges.

Remove the pancake from the oven. Slice into wedges and serve immediately.

= For serving (optional) =

Top with @maple syrup{}, @fruit preserves{}, @powdered sugar{}, or
@cinnamon sugar{}, as desired.
